<stack-static>
    <statement><p><p><m>A = {\{2, 5, 8, 11\}}</m> and <m>B = {\{11, 8, 5, 2\}}</m>.</p><p>(a) Which is true?</p><p>[ A and B are equal (so also equivalent). | A and B are equivalent but not equal. | A and B are not equivalent. ]  </p><p>(b) Write a set <m>C</m> of whole numbers less than <m>30</m> that is equivalent to <m>A</m> but not equal to <m>A</m>.</p><p><fillin characters="25" name="ans2"/>  </p></p></statement>
    <solution><p><p>(a) <m>A = {\{2, 5, 8, 11\}}</m> has <m>{4}</m> elements and <m>B = {\{2, 5, 8, 11\}}</m> has <m>{4}</m>. They have exactly the same elements, so they are equal (and so also equivalent).</p><p>(b) <m>C</m> needs <m>{4}</m> elements, like <m>A</m>, but must differ from <m>A</m> in at least one element. For example <m>C = {\{26, 27, 28, 29\}}</m>. Many other answers are correct.</p></p></solution>
    <answer><p>A and B are equal (so also equivalent).</p></answer>
    <answer><p><m>\left \{26 , 27 , 28 , 29 \right \}</m></p></answer>
</stack-static>